Question: Can you solve this in O(1) space?
Answer: Yes, by using the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm, which only requires two variables (a candidate and a counter) instead of a whole hash map.

5. WHAT I SHOULD REMEMBER (for my revision notes)

* The key insight, in one sentence: A majority element is so common that it will always outlast all other different elements if they cancel each other out one-by-one.
* My mistakes, as a short checklist for next time: You made no logic mistakes. For cleaner code, try using a range-based for loop (for int num : nums) instead of a standard index loop.
